*PPD-Adobe: "4.3"
*% SYNTHETIC FIXTURE - hand-written for testing ppdprobe.py.
*% Not derived from any vendor PPD. Models a driver that DOES provide an
*% identity escape on its ICC qualifier (a "None" value resolving to a
*% working-space profile rather than a paper profile).
*FormatVersion: "4.3"
*ModelName: "Example Inkjet With Escape"
*NickName: "Example Inkjet With Escape"
*ColorDevice: True
*cupsFilter: "application/vnd.cups-raster 0 /path/to/vendor/filter"

*OpenUI *XXColorMatch/Color Matching: PickOne
*DefaultXXColorMatch: 3
*XXColorMatch 1/Vendor Color Controls: ""
*XXColorMatch 2/ColorSync: ""
*XXColorMatch 3/Off (No Color Adjustment): ""
*CloseUI: *XXColorMatch

*cupsICCQualifier3: XXProfileSpec
*OpenUI *XXProfileSpec/Vendor Profile: PickOne
*DefaultXXProfileSpec: 0
*XXProfileSpec 0/None: ""
*XXProfileSpec 1/Example Glossy: ""
*XXProfileSpec 2/Example Matte: ""
*CloseUI: *XXProfileSpec

*cupsICCProfile ..0/sRGB Profile: "/System/Library/ColorSync/Profiles/sRGB Profile.icc"
*cupsICCProfile ..1/Example Glossy: "/path/to/vendor/ExampleGlossy.icc"
*cupsICCProfile ..2/Example Matte: "/path/to/vendor/ExampleMatte.icc"

*APSupportsCustomColorMatching: True
*APCustomColorMatchingProfile sRGB/sRGB: "sRGB"
*APCustomColorMatchingProfile AdobeRGB/AdobeRGB: "AdobeRGB"
